syntax:
For a class with virtual functions, the syntax involves declaring functions as 'virtual' in the base class:
class Base {
public:
    virtual void func() {};  // Virtual function
    int data;  // Non-static data member
    // Implementation note: The object layout includes a vptr before 'data'
};
class Derived : public Base {
public:
    void func() override {};  // Overrides the virtual function
    // Note: Derived's vtable will have its own entry for func()
};
